  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 2. The images of the pins formed when we see through the prism are
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: When we see the pins through the prism, we see the refracted rays,
    and these refracted rays appear to come from the images of the pins and hence
    we can say that the images of real objects are always virtual and erect.
  options:
  - real and inverted
  - virtual and erect
  - real and erect
  - virtual and Inverted
  correctOptionIndex: 1
